  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EU Funded Southern Colombia Uprooted People&apos;s Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is a three-year 1.3m Euro programme funded by the European Union to improve the living conditions of 512 displaced and vulnerable families in the dioceses of  Neiva, Garz&#xf3;n and Florencia in Southern Colombia. There are three components to the programme (a) Community strengthening, legal aid and psycho-social support (b) setting up 24 small community businesses (c) advocacy and communications work. The programme also aims to integrate private and public assistance to the communities into a sustainable and replicable model. The programme is based on CAFOD&#x2019;s ten years of support for the local Church and we see it as a platform for a further programme in this region.</narrative>
  </description>
